---
import Shell from "../layouts/Shell.astro";
const experiments=[{n:"01",title:"Spring / response",desc:"A compact motion study. Trigger the spring, change its tension and watch the interface settle.",status:"INTERACTIVE"},{n:"02",title:"Type / scale",desc:"A responsive type specimen that changes with the viewport instead of forcing fixed line lengths.",status:"RESPONSIVE"},{n:"03",title:"Touch / intent",desc:"A gesture surface with pointer and keyboard input. It stays usable without hover.",status:"INPUT STUDY"},{n:"04",title:"Reduced motion",desc:"The same page respects the operating-system preference and removes non-essential movement.",status:"ACCESSIBILITY"}];
---
<Shell title="Lab — Vinith Reddy Banda" description="Interactive experiments in motion, responsive type and input design.">
<section class="page-hero section-pad"><div class="section-index"><span>THE LABORATORY</span><span>LIVE EXPERIMENTS / NO. 004</span></div><p class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-mark"></span> SMALL STUDIES / WORKING PROTOTYPES</p><h1 class="page-heading">Test the<br/><em>details.</em></h1><p class="page-deck">Small, usable experiments. Each one isolates a behaviour so the interaction can be felt, tested and improved.</p></section>
<section class="lab-feature section-pad"><div class="section-index"><span>01 / SPRING RESPONSE</span><span>PRESS TO RUN</span></div><div class="lab-playground"><div class="lab-playground-copy"><span class="micro-label">MOTION STUDY / 001</span><h2>Movement<br/><em>with purpose.</em></h2><p>One deliberate spring, no endless background animation. Trigger it when you want to inspect the response.</p><button type="button" class="lab-run" id="lab-motion-trigger">RUN THE MOTION <span>↗</span></button></div><button type="button" class="lab-motion-stage" id="lab-motion-stage" aria-label="Trigger the spring motion"><span class="lab-motion-ring"></span><span class="lab-motion-core">V.</span><small>TAP / CLICK TO REPLAY</small></button></div><div class="lab-slider-row"><label for="motion-intensity">SPRING INTENSITY</label><input id="motion-intensity" type="range" min="1" max="5" value="3"/><output id="motion-intensity-value">03 / BALANCED</output></div></section>
<section class="lab-list-section section-pad"><div class="section-index"><span>02 / NOTEBOOK</span><span>DESIGN & ENGINEERING</span></div>{experiments.map(x=><article class="lab-row"><span>{x.n}</span><div><h2>{x.title}</h2><p>{x.desc}</p></div><span class="lab-status">{x.status}</span></article>)}</section><section class="lab-note section-pad"><span class="micro-label">THE RULE</span><p>Motion should explain a change, reward an action or help someone understand where they are. If it does none of those, it can leave.</p></section></Shell>